iting it.\",\n  \"capped\": [],\n  \"hits\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H001\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 67,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H002\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 86,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H003\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 135,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H004\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 152,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H005\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P31\",\n      \"item\": \"B02\",\n      \"title\": \"Wildcard IAM or RBAC grant\",\n      \"file\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf\",\n      \"line\": 100,\n      \"text\": \"Resource = \\\"*\\\"\",\n      \"ask\": \"Is this grant attached to the agent's identity? A wildcard action or resource gives it operations beyond the named ones the task needs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H006\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P40\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"title\": \"Audit write inside a try block\",\n      \"file\": \"src/agent/loop.ts\",\n      \"line\": 37,\n      \"text\": \"\",\n      \"ask\": \"Is the audit record written only after the action succeeds? Check the deny, error, and exception branches also record the attempt, and that an audit failure doesn't silently pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H007\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P40\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"title\": \"Audit write inside a try block\",\n      \"file\": \"src/agent/loop.ts\",\n      \"line\": 38,\n      \"text\": \"try {\",\n      \"ask\": \"Is the audit record written only after the action succeeds? Check the deny, error, and exception branches also record the attempt, and that an audit failure doesn't silently pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H008\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P40\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"title\": \"Audit write inside a try block\",\n      \"file\": \"src/agent/loop.ts\",\n      \"line\": 106,\n      \"text\": \"try {\",\n      \"ask\": \"Is the audit record written only after the action succeeds? Check the deny, error, and exception branches also record the attempt, and that an audit failure doesn't silently pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H009\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P40\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"title\": \"Audit write inside a try block\",\n      \"file\": \"src/tools/executor.ts\",\n      \"line\": 84,\n      \"text\": \"\",\n      \"ask\": \"Is the audit record written only after the action succeeds? Check the deny, error, and exception branches also record the attempt, and that an audit failure doesn't silently pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H010\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P40\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"title\": \"Audit write inside a try block\",\n      \"file\": \"src/tools/executor.ts\",\n      \"line\": 85,\n      \"text\": \"try {\",\n      \"ask\": \"Is the audit record written only after the action succeeds? Check the deny, error, and exception branches also record the attempt, and that an audit failure doesn't silently pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H011\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P50\",\n      \"item\": \"E03\",\n      \"title\": \"Tool list loaded from server\",\n      \"file\": \"src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts\",\n      \"line\": 78,\n      \"text\": \"c.listTools(),\",\n      \"ask\": \"After loading, are each tool's description and schema compared against an approved fingerprint, so a changed tool is blocked rather than passed to the model?\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n37:- A vendor service dropping agent or tenant identity from its records → **E10**\n422:- Run can't be rebuilt across gateway, tool services, and delegated workers → **E10**\n561:- No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type → **E12**\n590:## E10 · G1 · C9/Obs-T1 — Audit across service boundaries\n614:- **E10.1** The gateway, tool services, and delegated workers each write audit records with all six identity fields and the shared trace context.\n616:- **E10.2** The agent's credentials have no permission to delete, update, or overwrite audit records (for example an append-only or WORM store with IAM denies).\n618:- **E10.3** No tool or peer the agent can call is able to delete or rewrite audit records on its behalf, or such requests are held for approval under B05.\n620:- **E10.4** Calls into vendor services are mapped from the gateway's verified identity and correlation ID to the vendor's job or receipt ID.\n627:- Audit retention, access, redaction, or export rules missing → **E11**\n654:**Needs runtime evidence:** Needs the E10 test: merge logs across services into one graph with all six fields, and show deletes or edits by the agent, directly or through a more powerful tool or peer, are denied or held for approval.\n{\n  \"id\": \"E10.1\",\n  \"check\": \"The gateway, tool services, and delegated workers each write audit records with all six identity fields and the shared trace context.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find audit writers in the gateway, tool services, and delegated workers. 2) Check each writes all six identity fields and the shared trace context. 3) Answer no if any component writes records without them or starts a new trace. Answer unknown if a component's code is outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JyR3BAd1BKkuovBHXU9NtQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdQFsg4utGxTK8fKw3B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X7h1Q822EKwQ8eLWMs9WjD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-rbt3823l/agent; cat src/audit/recorder.ts src/agent/identity.ts infra/terraform/iam.tf infra/terraform/main.tf config/policy.yaml"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2280,"cache_read_input_tokens":22881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2280},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be07f175-8066-4c39-92f7-e712df5d0616","uuid":"14dbb759-15a6-446d-8a24-b9cb73847b52","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:14:29.768Z","request_id":"req_011CgDdQFGxavnC9wNT9qtCa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01X7h1Q822EKwQ8eLWMs9WjD":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-rbt3823l/agent; cat src/audit/recorder.ts src/agent/identity.ts infra/terraform/iam.tf infra/terraform/main.tf config/policy.yaml"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X7h1Q822EKwQ8eLWMs9WjD","type":"tool_result","content":"import { FirehoseClient, PutRecordCommand } from \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\";\nimport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { env } from \"../config.js\";\n\n// Every audit record carries the six identity fields. Values come from RunContext, which is built\n// by the HTTP layer and the worker, never from model output.\nexport const IdentityFields = z.object({\n  accountableParty: z.string().min(1),\n  operationalOwner: z.string().min(1),\n  tenantId: z.string().min(1),\n  agentTypeId: z.string().startsWith(\"sha256:\"),\n  agentInstanceId: z.string().uuid(),\n  traceparent: z.string().regex(/^00-[0-9a-f]{32}-[0-9a-f]{16}-0[01]$/),\n});\n\nexport const AuditEvent = IdentityFields.extend({\n  eventId: z.string().uuid(),\n  ts: z.string().datetime(),\n  runId: z.string().uuid(),\n  event: z.enum([\n    \"run.started\",\n    \"run.stopped\",\n    \"run.completed\",\n    \"intent.classified\",\n    \"model.decision\",\n    \"tool.denied\",\n    \"tool.approval_requested\",\n    \"tool.executed\",\n    \"tool.failed\",\n    \"payment.refund\",\n    \"peer.call\",\n    \"reminder.sent\",\n  ]),\n  subject: z.object({ kind: z.enum([\"patient\", \"staff\", \"system\"]), id: z.string() }),\n  tool: z.string().optional(),\n  toolUseId: z.string().optional(),\n  policyVersion: z.string().optional(),\n  approvalId: z.string().optional(),\n  reason: z.string().optional(),\n  context: z\n    .object({\n      tokens: z.number().int().nonnegative().nullable(),\n      status: z.enum([\"measured\", \"estimated\", \"unavailable\"]),\n      method: z.string(),\n      cachedInputTokens: z.number().int().nonnegative().nullable(),\n      compacted: z.boolean(),\n    })\n    .optional(),\n  detail: z.record(z.unknown()).optional(),\n});\nexport type AuditEvent = z.infer<typeof AuditEvent>;\n\nconst firehose = new FirehoseClient({ region: env.region });\n\nexport class AuditUnavailable extends Error {}\n\nexport const audit = {\n  async record(e: Omit<AuditEvent, \"eventId\" | \"ts\">): Promise<void> {\n    const full = AuditEvent.parse({ ...e, eventId: randomUUID(), ts: new Date().toISOString() });\n    try {\n      await firehose.send(\n        new PutRecordCommand({\n          DeliveryStreamName: env.auditStream,\n          Record: { Data: Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(full) + \"\\n\") },\n        }),\n      );\n    } catch (err) {\n      // Callers treat this as a hard failure: an action that cannot be audited does not run.\n      throw new AuditUnavailable(`audit delivery failed: ${(err as Error).message}`);\n    }\n  },\n};\n\n// PHI scrubbing for anything that leaves the EHR boundary toward the model or the audit summary.\nconst DROP_KEYS = new Set([\"ssn\", \"dateOfBirth\", \"dob\", \"memberId\", \"subscriberId\", \"cardNumber\", \"cardLast4\", \"address\"]);\nconst PATTERNS: Array<[RegExp, string]> = [\n  [/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[ssn]\"],\n  [/\\b(?:\\d[ -]?){13,19}\\b/g, \"[card]\"],\n  [/\\b[A-Z]{3}\\d{9}\\b/g, \"[member-id]\"],\n];\n\nexport function redactPhi(value: unknown): unknown {\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    return PATTERNS.reduce((s, [re, sub]) => s.replace(re, sub), value);\n  }\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.map(redactPhi);\n  if (value && typeof value === \"object\") {\n    const out: Record<string, unknown> = {};\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(value)) {\n      if (DROP_KEYS.has(k)) continue;\n      out[k] = redactPhi(v);\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  return value;\n}\nimport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { ROOT, AGENT_MODEL, CLASSIFIER_MODEL, env } from \"../config.js\";\n\n// agent-type-id = sha256 over a fixed, ordered manifest of identity-defining inputs.\n// Each input is written as \"<label>\\0<bytes>\\0\" so that inputs cannot run together.\nconst CONFIG_FILES = [\"config/policy.yaml\", \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\", \"config/budgets.yaml\"];\n\nexport interface TypeIdInputs {\n  imageDigest: string;\n  harnessVersion: string;\n  harnessGitSha: string;\n}\n\nexport function typeIdManifest(inputs: TypeIdInputs): Array<[string, Buffer]> {\n  const parts: Array<[string, Buffer]> = [\n    [\"image\", Buffer.from(inputs.imageDigest)],\n    [\"harness.version\", Buffer.from(inputs.harnessVersion)],\n    [\"harness.gitSha\", Buffer.from(inputs.harnessGitSha)],\n  ];\n  const promptDir = join(ROOT, \"prompts\");\n  const promptFiles = readdirSync(promptDir)\n    .filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))\n    .sort();\n  for (const f of promptFiles) {\n    parts.push([`prompt:${f}`, readFileSync(join(promptDir, f))]);\n  }\n  parts.push([\"model.agent\", Buffer.from(AGENT_MODEL)]);\n  parts.push([\"model.classifier\", Buffer.from(CLASSIFIER_MODEL)]);\n  for (const f of CONFIG_FILES) {\n    parts.push([`config:${f}`, readFileSync(join(ROOT, f))]);\n  }\n  return parts;\n}\n\nexport function computeAgentTypeId(inputs: TypeIdInputs): string {\n  const h = createHash(\"sha256\");\n  for (const [label, bytes] of typeIdManifest(inputs)) {\n    h.update(label);\n    h.update(\"\\0\");\n    h.update(bytes);\n    h.update(\"\\0\");\n  }\n  return `sha256:${h.digest(\"hex\")}`;\n}\n\n// One instance id per process. Pods are the unit an operator contains.\nexport const AGENT_INSTANCE_ID = randomUUID();\n\nlet AGENT_TYPE_ID = \"\";\nexport function setAgentTypeId(id: string): void {\n  AGENT_TYPE_ID = id;\n}\n\nexport interface Subject {\n  kind: \"patient\" | \"staff\" | \"system\";\n  id: string;\n}\n\nexport interface Logger {\n  info(obj: object, msg?: string): void;\n  warn(obj: object, msg?: string): void;\n  error(obj: object, msg?: string): void;\n}\n\nexport interface RunContext {\n  runId: string;\n  tenantId: string;\n  subject: Subject;\n  channel: \"sms\" | \"webchat\" | \"reminder\";\n  traceparent: string;\n  log: Logger;\n  identity(): {\n    accountableParty: string;\n    operationalOwner: string;\n    tenantId: string;\n    agentTypeId: string;\n    agentInstanceId: string;\n    traceparent: string;\n  };\n  workloadToken(): Promise<string>;\n}\n\n// Projected service-account token (audience: the group STS), rotated by the kubelet.\nconst WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH = process.env.WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH ?? \"/var/run/secrets/tokens/sts-token\";\n\nexport function newRunContext(init: {\n  tenantId: string;\n  subject: Subject;\n  channel: RunContext[\"channel\"];\n  traceparent?: string;\n  log: Logger;\n}): RunContext {\n  const runId = randomUUID();\n  const traceparent = init.traceparent ?? `00-${randomUUID().replace(/-/g, \"\")}-${randomUUID().replace(/-/g, \"\").slice(0, 16)}-01`;\n  return {\n    runId,\n    tenantId: init.tenantId,\n    subject: init.subject,\n    channel: init.channel,\n    traceparent,\n    log: init.log,\n    identity: () => ({\n      accountableParty: env.accountableParty,\n      operationalOwner: env.operationalOwner,\n      tenantId: init.tenantId,\n      agentTypeId: AGENT_TYPE_ID,\n      agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID,\n      traceparent,\n    }),\n    workloadToken: async () => readFileSync(WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH, \"utf8\").trim(),\n  };\n}\n# Runtime identity for the agent pods (IRSA). This role belongs to the agent, not to any user:\n# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not touch theirs.\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {\n  name                 = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n  max_session_duration = 3600\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { Federated = module.eks.oidc_provider_arn }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringEquals = {\n          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:sub\" = [\n            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent\",\n            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent-reminders\",\n          ]\n          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n        }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"runtime\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n  role = aws_iam_role.runtime.id\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [\n      {\n        Sid      = \"ReadClinicSecrets\"\n        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n        Action   = [\"secretsmanager:GetSecretValue\"]\n        Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"\n      },\n      {\n        Sid    = \"AgentState\"\n        Effect = \"Allow\"\n        Action = [\n          \"dynamodb:GetItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:BatchGetItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:PutItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:Query\",\n        ]\n        Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"\n      },\n      {\n        Sid      = \"Audit\"\n        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n        Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]\n        Resource = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.audit.arn\n      },\n    ]\n  })\n}\n\n# Operators who may stop the agent. Assumable only through SSO by the on-call group.\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { AWS = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root\" }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringLike = { \"aws:PrincipalArn\" = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/*/AWSReservedSSO_AgentPlatformOnCall_*\" }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n  role = aws_iam_role.ops_killswitch.id\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n      Action   = [\"dynamodb:PutItem\", \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\", \"dynamodb:GetItem\"]\n      Resource = aws_dynamodb_table.control.arn\n    }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"firehose\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-audit-firehose\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version   = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{ Effect = \"Allow\", Principal = { Service = \"firehose.amazonaws.com\" }, Action = \"sts:AssumeRole\" }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"firehose\" {\n  name = \"write-audit-bucket\"\n  role = aws_iam_role.firehose.id\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n      Action   = [\"s3:PutObject\", \"s3:AbortMultipartUpload\", \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"]\n      Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn, \"${aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn}/*\"]\n    }]\n  })\n}\nterraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.9.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    aws    = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 6.14\" }\n    github = { source = \"integrations/github\", version = \"~> 6.6\" }\n  }\n  backend \"s3\" {\n    bucket         = \"northbay-tfstate-418295730611\"\n    key            = \"clinic-agent/prod.tfstate\"\n    region         = \"us-west-2\"\n    dynamodb_table = \"northbay-tf-locks\"\n    encrypt        = true\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"aws\" {\n  region = var.region\n  default_tags {\n    tags = { app = \"clinic-agent\", owner = \"agent-platform\", data = \"phi\" }\n  }\n}\n\nvariable \"region\" {\n  type    = string\n  default = \"us-west-2\"\n}\n\nvariable \"clinic_ids\" {\n  type    = list(string)\n  default = [\"nb-castro\", \"nb-fremont\", \"nb-oakland\", \"nb-sanmateo\", \"nb-walnutcreek\"]\n}\n\ndata \"aws_caller_identity\" \"current\" {}\n\nmodule \"eks\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws\"\n  version = \"21.3.1\"\n\n  name               = \"clinic-agent-prod\"\n  kubernetes_version = \"1.33\"\n  vpc_id             = module.vpc.vpc_id\n  subnet_ids         = module.vpc.private_subnets\n\n  endpoint_public_access = false\n  enable_irsa            = true\n\n  authentication_mode = \"API\"\n  access_entries = {\n    deploy = {\n      principal_arn = aws_iam_role.deploy.arn\n      policy_associations = {\n        ns = {\n          policy_arn   = \"arn:aws:eks::aws:cluster-access-policy/AmazonEKSEditPolicy\"\n          access_scope = { type = \"namespace\", namespaces = [\"clinic-agent\"] }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  eks_managed_node_groups = {\n    agents = {\n      instance_types = [\"m7g.large\"]\n      ami_type       = \"BOTTLEROCKET_ARM_64\"\n      min_size       = 2\n      max_size       = 6\n      desired_size   = 3\n      metadata_options = {\n        http_tokens                 = \"required\"\n        http_put_response_hop_limit = 1\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nmodule \"vpc\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws\"\n  version = \"6.4.0\"\n\n  name            = \"clinic-agent-prod\"\n  cidr            = \"10.42.0.0/16\"\n  azs             = [\"us-west-2a\", \"us-west-2b\", \"us-west-2c\"]\n  private_subnets = [\"10.42.1.0/24\", \"10.42.2.0/24\", \"10.42.3.0/24\"]\n  public_subnets  = [\"10.42.101.0/24\", \"10.42.102.0/24\", \"10.42.103.0/24\"]\n\n  enable_nat_gateway = true\n  single_nat_gateway = false\n}\n\nresource \"aws_ecr_repository\" \"agent\" {\n  name                 = \"clinic-agent\"\n  image_tag_mutability = \"IMMUTABLE\"\n  image_scanning_configuration { scan_on_push = true }\n}\n\n# State tables. Approvals are written by the staff console; budgets by the agent; the control\n# table holds the stop flags operators set.\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"approvals\" {\n  name         = \"clinic-agent-approvals\"\n  billing_mode = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"\n  hash_key     = \"id\"\n  attribute {\n    name = \"id\"\n    type = \"S\"\n  }\n  point_in_time_recovery { enabled = true }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"budgets\" {\n  name         = \"clinic-agent-budgets\"\n  billing_mode = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"\n  hash_key     = \"pk\"\n  attribute {\n    name = \"pk\"\n    type = \"S\"\n  }\n  ttl {\n    attribute_name = \"expiresAt\"\n    enabled        = true\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"control\" {\n  name         = \"clinic-agent-control\"\n  billing_mode = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"\n  hash_key     = \"pk\"\n  attribute {\n    name = \"pk\"\n    type = \"S\"\n  }\n  point_in_time_recovery { enabled = true }\n}\n\n# Audit: Firehose to an S3 bucket with object lock in compliance mode (7 years, HIPAA retention).\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"audit\" {\n  bucket              = \"clinic-agent-audit-${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}\"\n  object_lock_enabled = true\n}\n\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_object_lock_configuration\" \"audit\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.audit.id\n  rule {\n    default_retention {\n      mode  = \"COMPLIANCE\"\n      years = 7\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream\" \"audit\" {\n  name        = \"clinic-agent-audit\"\n  destination = \"extended_s3\"\n  extended_s3_configuration {\n    role_arn            = aws_iam_role.firehose.arn\n    bucket_arn          = aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn\n    prefix              = \"audit/dt=!{timestamp:yyyy-MM-dd}/\"\n    error_output_prefix = \"audit-errors/!{firehose:error-output-type}/\"\n    buffering_interval  = 60\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"ehr\" {\n  for_each = toset(concat(var.clinic_ids, [\"_catalog\"]))\n  name     = \"clinic-agent/ehr/${each.key}\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {\n  for_each = toset(var.clinic_ids)\n  name     = \"clinic-agent/payments/${each.key}\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"sms\" {\n  for_each = toset(var.clinic_ids)\n  name     = \"clinic-agent/sms/${each.key}\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"sms_signing\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent/sms-signing\"\n}\n# Action policy for the scheduling agent. Changes need agent-platform-leads review (CODEOWNERS).\npolicyVersion: \"2026-09-18.3\"\n\n# Tools that never run without a staff approval bound to the request.\nhighImpactTools:\n  - ehr__cancel_appointment\n  - payments__refund_deposit\n  - sms__send_freeform\n\napproval:\n  ttlSeconds: 900\n  approverRoles:\n    - front_desk_lead\n    - clinic_manager\n  # Approvals are recorded in DynamoDB table clinic-agent-approvals.\n  table: clinic-agent-approvals","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be07f175-8066-4c39-92f7-e712df5d0616","uuid":"c33a45c3-b7dc-449b-9a09-98c626a0760e","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:14:29.831Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import { FirehoseClient, PutRecordCommand } from \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\";\nimport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { env } from \"../config.js\";\n\n// Every audit record carries the six identity fields. Values come from RunContext, which is built\n// by the HTTP layer and the worker, never from model output.\nexport const IdentityFields = z.object({\n  accountableParty: z.string().min(1),\n  operationalOwner: z.string().min(1),\n  tenantId: z.string().min(1),\n  agentTypeId: z.string().startsWith(\"sha256:\"),\n  agentInstanceId: z.string().uuid(),\n  traceparent: z.string().regex(/^00-[0-9a-f]{32}-[0-9a-f]{16}-0[01]$/),\n});\n\nexport const AuditEvent = IdentityFields.extend({\n  eventId: z.string().uuid(),\n  ts: z.string().datetime(),\n  runId: z.string().uuid(),\n  event: z.enum([\n    \"run.started\",\n    \"run.stopped\",\n    \"run.completed\",\n    \"intent.classified\",\n    \"model.decision\",\n    \"tool.denied\",\n    \"tool.approval_requested\",\n    \"tool.executed\",\n    \"tool.failed\",\n    \"payment.refund\",\n    \"peer.call\",\n    \"reminder.sent\",\n  ]),\n  subject: z.object({ kind: z.enum([\"patient\", \"staff\", \"system\"]), id: z.string() }),\n  tool: z.string().optional(),\n  toolUseId: z.string().optional(),\n  policyVersion: z.string().optional(),\n  approvalId: z.string().optional(),\n  reason: z.string().optional(),\n  context: z\n    .object({\n      tokens: z.number().int().nonnegative().nullable(),\n      status: z.enum([\"measured\", \"estimated\", \"unavailable\"]),\n      method: z.string(),\n      cachedInputTokens: z.number().int().nonnegative().nullable(),\n      compacted: z.boolean(),\n    })\n    .optional(),\n  detail: z.record(z.unknown()).optional(),\n});\nexport type AuditEvent = z.infer<typeof AuditEvent>;\n\nconst firehose = new FirehoseClient({ region: env.region });\n\nexport class AuditUnavailable extends Error {}\n\nexport const audit = {\n  async record(e: Omit<AuditEvent, \"eventId\" | \"ts\">): Promise<void> {\n    const full = AuditEvent.parse({ ...e, eventId: randomUUID(), ts: new Date().toISOString() });\n    try {\n      await firehose.send(\n        new PutRecordCommand({\n          DeliveryStreamName: env.auditStream,\n          Record: { Data: Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(full) + \"\\n\") },\n        }),\n      );\n    } catch (err) {\n      // Callers treat this as a hard failure: an action that cannot be audited does not run.\n      throw new AuditUnavailable(`audit delivery failed: ${(err as Error).message}`);\n    }\n  },\n};\n\n// PHI scrubbing for anything that leaves the EHR boundary toward the model or the audit summary.\nconst DROP_KEYS = new Set([\"ssn\", \"dateOfBirth\", \"dob\", \"memberId\", \"subscriberId\", \"cardNumber\", \"cardLast4\", \"address\"]);\nconst PATTERNS: Array<[RegExp, string]> = [\n  [/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, \"[ssn]\"],\n  [/\\b(?:\\d[ -]?){13,19}\\b/g, \"[card]\"],\n  [/\\b[A-Z]{3}\\d{9}\\b/g, \"[member-id]\"],\n];\n\nexport function redactPhi(value: unknown): unknown {\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    return PATTERNS.reduce((s, [re, sub]) => s.replace(re, sub), value);\n  }\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.map(redactPhi);\n  if (value && typeof value === \"object\") {\n    const out: Record<string, unknown> = {};\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(value)) {\n      if (DROP_KEYS.has(k)) continue;\n      out[k] = redactPhi(v);\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  return value;\n}\nimport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { ROOT, AGENT_MODEL, CLASSIFIER_MODEL, env } from \"../config.js\";\n\n// agent-type-id = sha256 over a fixed, ordered manifest of identity-defining inputs.\n// Each input is written as \"<label>\\0<bytes>\\0\" so that inputs cannot run together.\nconst CONFIG_FILES = [\"config/policy.yaml\", \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\", \"config/budgets.yaml\"];\n\nexport interface TypeIdInputs {\n  imageDigest: string;\n  harnessVersion: string;\n  harnessGitSha: string;\n}\n\nexport function typeIdManifest(inputs: TypeIdInputs): Array<[string, Buffer]> {\n  const parts: Array<[string, Buffer]> = [\n    [\"image\", Buffer.from(inputs.imageDigest)],\n    [\"harness.version\", Buffer.from(inputs.harnessVersion)],\n    [\"harness.gitSha\", Buffer.from(inputs.harnessGitSha)],\n  ];\n  const promptDir = join(ROOT, \"prompts\");\n  const promptFiles = readdirSync(promptDir)\n    .filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))\n    .sort();\n  for (const f of promptFiles) {\n    parts.push([`prompt:${f}`, readFileSync(join(promptDir, f))]);\n  }\n  parts.push([\"model.agent\", Buffer.from(AGENT_MODEL)]);\n  parts.push([\"model.classifier\", Buffer.from(CLASSIFIER_MODEL)]);\n  for (const f of CONFIG_FILES) {\n    parts.push([`config:${f}`, readFileSync(join(ROOT, f))]);\n  }\n  return parts;\n}\n\nexport function computeAgentTypeId(inputs: TypeIdInputs): string {\n  const h = createHash(\"sha256\");\n  for (const [label, bytes] of typeIdManifest(inputs)) {\n    h.update(label);\n    h.update(\"\\0\");\n    h.update(bytes);\n    h.update(\"\\0\");\n  }\n  return `sha256:${h.digest(\"hex\")}`;\n}\n\n// One instance id per process. Pods are the unit an operator contains.\nexport const AGENT_INSTANCE_ID = randomUUID();\n\nlet AGENT_TYPE_ID = \"\";\nexport function setAgentTypeId(id: string): void {\n  AGENT_TYPE_ID = id;\n}\n\nexport interface Subject {\n  kind: \"patient\" | \"staff\" | \"system\";\n  id: string;\n}\n\nexport interface Logger {\n  info(obj: object, msg?: string): void;\n  warn(obj: object, msg?: string): void;\n  error(obj: object, msg?: string): void;\n}\n\nexport interface RunContext {\n  runId: string;\n  tenantId: string;\n  subject: Subject;\n  channel: \"sms\" | \"webchat\" | \"reminder\";\n  traceparent: string;\n  log: Logger;\n  identity(): {\n    accountableParty: string;\n    operationalOwner: string;\n    tenantId: string;\n    agentTypeId: string;\n    agentInstanceId: string;\n    traceparent: string;\n  };\n  workloadToken(): Promise<string>;\n}\n\n// Projected service-account token (audience: the group STS), rotated by the kubelet.\nconst WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH = process.env.WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH ?? \"/var/run/secrets/tokens/sts-token\";\n\nexport function newRunContext(init: {\n  tenantId: string;\n  subject: Subject;\n  channel: RunContext[\"channel\"];\n  traceparent?: string;\n  log: Logger;\n}): RunContext {\n  const runId = randomUUID();\n  const traceparent = init.traceparent ?? `00-${randomUUID().replace(/-/g, \"\")}-${randomUUID().replace(/-/g, \"\").slice(0, 16)}-01`;\n  return {\n    runId,\n    tenantId: init.tenantId,\n    subject: init.subject,\n    channel: init.channel,\n    traceparent,\n    log: init.log,\n    identity: () => ({\n      accountableParty: env.accountableParty,\n      operationalOwner: env.operationalOwner,\n      tenantId: init.tenantId,\n      agentTypeId: AGENT_TYPE_ID,\n      agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID,\n      traceparent,\n    }),\n    workloadToken: async () => readFileSync(WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH, \"utf8\").trim(),\n  };\n}\n# Runtime identity for the agent pods (IRSA). This role belongs to the agent, not to any user:\n# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not touch theirs.\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {\n  name                 = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n  max_session_duration = 3600\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { Federated = module.eks.oidc_provider_arn }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringEquals = {\n          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:sub\" = [\n            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent\",\n            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent-reminders\",\n          ]\n          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n        }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"runtime\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n  role = aws_iam_role.runtime.id\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [\n      {\n        Sid      = \"ReadClinicSecrets\"\n        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n        Action   = [\"secretsmanager:GetSecretValue\"]\n        Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"\n      },\n      {\n        Sid    = \"AgentState\"\n        Effect = \"Allow\"\n        Action = [\n          \"dynamodb:GetItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:BatchGetItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:PutItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\",\n          \"dynamodb:Query\",\n        ]\n        Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"\n      },\n      {\n        Sid      = \"Audit\"\n        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n        Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]\n        Resource = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.audit.arn\n      },\n    ]\n  })\n}\n\n# Operators who may stop the agent. Assumable only through SSO by the on-call group.\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { AWS = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root\" }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringLike = { \"aws:PrincipalArn\" = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/*/AWSReservedSSO_AgentPlatformOnCall_*\" }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n  role = aws_iam_role.ops_killswitch.id\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n      Action   = [\"dynamodb:PutItem\", \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\", \"dynamodb:GetItem\"]\n      Resource = aws_dynamodb_table.control.arn\n    }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"firehose\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent-audit-firehose\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version   = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{ Effect = \"Allow\", Principal = { Service = \"firehose.amazonaws.com\" }, Action = \"sts:AssumeRole\" }]\n  })\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"firehose\" {\n  name = \"write-audit-bucket\"\n  role = aws_iam_role.firehose.id\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n      Action   = [\"s3:PutObject\", \"s3:AbortMultipartUpload\", \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"]\n      Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn, \"${aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn}/*\"]\n    }]\n  })\n}\nterraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.9.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    aws    = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 6.14\" }\n    github = { source = \"integrations/github\", version = \"~> 6.6\" }\n  }\n  backend \"s3\" {\n    bucket         = \"northbay-tfstate-418295730611\"\n    key            = \"clinic-agent/prod.tfstate\"\n    region         = \"us-west-2\"\n    dynamodb_table = \"northbay-tf-locks\"\n    encrypt        = true\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"aws\" {\n  region = var.region\n  default_tags {\n    tags = { app = \"clinic-agent\", owner = \"agent-platform\", data = \"phi\" }\n  }\n}\n\nvariable \"region\" {\n  type    = string\n  default = \"us-west-2\"\n}\n\nvariable \"clinic_ids\" {\n  type    = list(string)\n  default = [\"nb-castro\", \"nb-fremont\", \"nb-oakland\", \"nb-sanmateo\", \"nb-walnutcreek\"]\n}\n\ndata \"aws_caller_identity\" \"current\" {}\n\nmodule \"eks\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws\"\n  version = \"21.3.1\"\n\n  name               = \"clinic-agent-prod\"\n  kubernetes_version = \"1.33\"\n  vpc_id             = module.vpc.vpc_id\n  subnet_ids         = module.vpc.private_subnets\n\n  endpoint_public_access = false\n  enable_irsa            = true\n\n  authentication_mode = \"API\"\n  access_entries = {\n    deploy = {\n      principal_arn = aws_iam_role.deploy.arn\n      policy_associations = {\n        ns = {\n          policy_arn   = \"arn:aws:eks::aws:cluster-access-policy/AmazonEKSEditPolicy\"\n          access_scope = { type = \"namespace\", namespaces = [\"clinic-agent\"] }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  eks_managed_node_groups = {\n    agents = {\n      instance_types = [\"m7g.large\"]\n      ami_type       = \"BOTTLEROCKET_ARM_64\"\n      min_size       = 2\n      max_size       = 6\n      desired_size   = 3\n      metadata_options = {\n        http_tokens                 = \"required\"\n        http_put_response_hop_limit = 1\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nmodule \"vpc\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws\"\n  version = \"6.4.0\"\n\n  name            = \"clinic-agent-prod\"\n  cidr            = \"10.42.0.0/16\"\n  azs             = [\"us-west-2a\", \"us-west-2b\", \"us-west-2c\"]\n  private_subnets = [\"10.42.1.0/24\", \"10.42.2.0/24\", \"10.42.3.0/24\"]\n  public_subnets  = [\"10.42.101.0/24\", \"10.42.102.0/24\", \"10.42.103.0/24\"]\n\n  enable_nat_gateway = true\n  single_nat_gateway = false\n}\n\nresource \"aws_ecr_repository\" \"agent\" {\n  name                 = \"clinic-agent\"\n  image_tag_mutability = \"IMMUTABLE\"\n  image_scanning_configuration { scan_on_push = true }\n}\n\n# State tables. Approvals are written by the staff console; budgets by the agent; the control\n# table holds the stop flags operators set.\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"approvals\" {\n  name         = \"clinic-agent-approvals\"\n  billing_mode = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"\n  hash_key     = \"id\"\n  attribute {\n    name = \"id\"\n    type = \"S\"\n  }\n  point_in_time_recovery { enabled = true }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"budgets\" {\n  name         = \"clinic-agent-budgets\"\n  billing_mode = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"\n  hash_key     = \"pk\"\n  attribute {\n    name = \"pk\"\n    type = \"S\"\n  }\n  ttl {\n    attribute_name = \"expiresAt\"\n    enabled        = true\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"control\" {\n  name         = \"clinic-agent-control\"\n  billing_mode = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"\n  hash_key     = \"pk\"\n  attribute {\n    name = \"pk\"\n    type = \"S\"\n  }\n  point_in_time_recovery { enabled = true }\n}\n\n# Audit: Firehose to an S3 bucket with object lock in compliance mode (7 years, HIPAA retention).\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"audit\" {\n  bucket              = \"clinic-agent-audit-${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}\"\n  object_lock_enabled = true\n}\n\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_object_lock_configuration\" \"audit\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.audit.id\n  rule {\n    default_retention {\n      mode  = \"COMPLIANCE\"\n      years = 7\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream\" \"audit\" {\n  name        = \"clinic-agent-audit\"\n  destination = \"extended_s3\"\n  extended_s3_configuration {\n    role_arn            = aws_iam_role.firehose.arn\n    bucket_arn          = aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn\n    prefix              = \"audit/dt=!{timestamp:yyyy-MM-dd}/\"\n    error_output_prefix = \"audit-errors/!{firehose:error-output-type}/\"\n    buffering_interval  = 60\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"ehr\" {\n  for_each = toset(concat(var.clinic_ids, [\"_catalog\"]))\n  name     = \"clinic-agent/ehr/${each.key}\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {\n  for_each = toset(var.clinic_ids)\n  name     = \"clinic-agent/payments/${each.key}\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"sms\" {\n  for_each = toset(var.clinic_ids)\n  name     = \"clinic-agent/sms/${each.key}\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"sms_signing\" {\n  name = \"clinic-agent/sms-signing\"\n}\n# Action policy for the scheduling agent. Changes need agent-platform-leads review (CODEOWNERS).\npolicyVersion: \"2026-09-18.3\"\n\n# Tools that never run without a staff approval bound to the request.\nhighImpactTools:\n  - ehr__cancel_appointment\n  - payments__refund_deposit\n  - sms__send_freeform\n\napproval:\n  ttlSeconds: 900\n  approverRoles:\n    - front_desk_lead\n    - clinic_manager\n  # Approvals are recorded in DynamoDB table clinic-agent-approvals.\n  table: clinic-agent-approvals","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X7h1Q822EKwQ8eLWMs9WjD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
