{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F6bKgcAnVjTCYmHcbgadDW","type":"tool_result","content":"561:- No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type → **E12**\n726:## E12 · G3 · C7/C8 — Fleet incident response\n777:**Needs runtime evidence:** Almost all of this item is shown by the E12 drill: mark a shared tool compromised, query the impact, quarantine, revoke, alert, and measure stop times. Code only shows that the controls exist.\n## E12 · G3 · C7/C8 — Fleet incident response\n\n**Lead:** Security. **Shares:** Operations, Governance, Business owner.\n\n### Requirement\n\nRun a drill where a shared tool or agent type is compromised. Find the affected instances and tenants. Quarantine the dependency, revoke the access involved, stop affected work, and alert the named responders. Check that alerts about abuse across agents, and about budgets, reach the team that can act. Name who decides whether to report outside the organization and share information.\n\n### Verification recipe\n\nMark a shared test tool or version as compromised. Query which instances and tenants it affects, quarantine it, revoke the access involved, and trigger response alerts. Affected work must stop within the set targets. Responders must get identities and traces they can act on. Record who decided on outside reporting and information sharing.\n\n**Evidence to keep:** Fleet impact query, quarantine and revocation records, alert delivery and response times.\n\n### Checks for likely_pass\n\nChecks for likely_pass:\n\n- (none) Code can't show this item. Don't rate it likely_pass; use needs_evidence, gap, or na_candidate.\n\n### Not covered here\n\nFile these problems under their owning item, not this one, unless this item's own requirement is also broken:\n\n- Kill switch for a single agent not drilled → **R11**\n- No owner named on each side of a shared control → **E01**\n- Tool or MCP server approved without vetting or pinning → **E02**\n- Budget and rate limits not enforced outside the model → **B07**\n\n### Heuristics\n\n**Provable from code:** no\n\n**Look for:**\n- An inventory or query that maps tool and dependency versions to instances and tenants.\n- Quarantine controls for a shared tool or agent type (gateway deny rule, registry block, feature flag).\n- Alert routes for cross-agent abuse and budget alerts to a named responder team.\n- An incident runbook that names who decides on outside reporting and information sharing.\n\n**Red flags:**\n- No way to find which deployments or tenants use a given tool version.\n- Quarantine requires a code change and full redeploy.\n- Alerts go to an unowned channel or a single person.\n- No named decision-maker for outside reporting.\n\n**Where to look:**\n- incident runbooks and on-call config\n- alert routing config (PagerDuty, Opsgenie, Alertmanager)\n- gateway and tool registry block rules\n- SBOM or dependency inventory systems\n\n**Needs runtime evidence:** Almost all of this item is shown by the E12 drill: mark a shared tool compromised, query the impact, quarantine, revoke, alert, and measure stop times. Code only shows that the controls exist.\n\n**N/A when:** never\n56:kind: CronJob\n63:  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n74:          restartPolicy: Never\n100:# Egress: DNS, the EHR MCP endpoint (private link), and the platform egress proxy only.\n104:kind: NetworkPolicy\n106:  name: clinic-agent-egress\n110:  policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]\n117:  egress:\n130:            matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }\n    20\t  deps: { registry: ToolRegistry; clinicById: (id: string) => { id: string; name: string } | undefined },\n    21\t): void {\n    22\t  app.post(\"/v1/chat\", { bodyLimit: 16_384 }, async (req, reply) => {\n    23\t    const auth = req.headers.authorization ?? \"\";\n    24\t    if (!auth.startsWith(\"Bearer \")) return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"missing token\" });\n    25\t\n    26\t    let claims: { sub: string; clinic_id: string; role: \"patient\" | \"staff\" };\n    27\t    try {\n    28\t      const { payload } = await jwtVerify(auth.slice(7), jwks, {\n    29\t        issuer: env.chatIssuer,\n    30\t        audience: \"clinic-agent-chat\",\n    31\t        algorithms: [\"ES256\"],\n    32\t        maxTokenAge: \"30m\",\n    33\t      });\n    34\t      claims = payload as unknown as typeof claims;\n    35\t    } catch {\n    36\t      return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"invalid token\" });\n    37\t    }\n    38\t\n    39\t    const body = ChatBody.safeParse(req.body);\n    40\t    if (!body.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \"invalid body\" });\n    41\t\n    42\t    // The group site embeds one widget for all clinics and sends the clinic the patient picked.\n    43\t    const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;\n    44\t    const clinic = deps.clinicById(tenantId);\n    45\t    if (!clinic) return reply.code(404).send({ error: \"unknown clinic\" });\n    46\t\n    47\t    const tp = req.headers.traceparent;\n    48\t    const ctx = newRunContext({\n    49\t      tenantId: clinic.id,\n    50\t      subject: { kind: claims.role === \"staff\" ? \"staff\" : \"patient\", id: claims.sub },\n    51\t      channel: \"webchat\",\n    52\t      traceparent: typeof tp === \"string\" && TRACEPARENT.test(tp) ? tp : undefined,\n    53\t      log: req.log,\n    54\t    });\n    55\t\n    56\t    const out = await runAgent(deps.registry, ctx, clinic, body.data.message);\n    57\t    return reply.send({ reply: out.text, handoff: out.handoff !== null, runId: ctx.runId });\n    58\t  });\n    59\t}\n  await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.started\", detail: { channel: ctx.channel } });\n\n  try {\n    await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n\n    const intent = await classifyIntent(anthropic, patientText);\n    await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });\n    if (intent.failure) ctx.log.warn({ classifier: intent.requestedModel, failure: intent.failure }, \"intent classifier control failure\");\n    if (intent.route === \"staff\") {\n      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason: `routed_to_staff:${intent.failure ?? intent.intent}` });\n      return { text: \"Thanks. A member of our front desk team will get back to you shortly.\", handoff: { reason: intent.failure ?? String(intent.intent) } };\n    }\n\n    const system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n    const tools = registry.definitions();\n    const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\n      { role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${escapeTags(patientText)}</patient_message>` },\n    ];\n\n    for (;;) {\n      budget.turn();\n      await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n\n      const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n      const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n      const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n      const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n      await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n\n      const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n      await audit.record({\n        ...ident(),\n        event: \"model.decision\",\n        context: contextSize,\n        detail: {\n          servedModel: res.model,\n          stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n          proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n          span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n        },\n      });\n\n      if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n        const text = res.content\n          .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n          .map((b) => b.text)\n          .join(\"\\n\")\n          .slice(0, 320);\n        await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.completed\" });\n        return { text, handoff: null };\n      }\n\n      messages.push({ role: \"assistant\", content: res.content });\n      const results: Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam[] = [];\n      for (const call of toolUses) {\n        results.push(await executeTool(registry, ctx, call, { contextSize, budget }));\n      }\n      messages.push({ role: \"user\", content: results });\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    const reason =\n      err instanceof BudgetExceeded\n        ? `budget:${err.limit}`\n        : err instanceof Halted\n          ? `halted:${err.scope}`\n          : err instanceof AuditUnavailable\n            ? \"audit_unavailable\"\n            : budget.signal.aborted\n              ? `aborted:${String((budget.signal.reason as Error)?.message ?? \"\")}`\n              : `error:${(err as Error).message.slice(0, 200)}`;\n    try {\n      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason });\n    } catch {\n      ctx.log.error({ runId: ctx.runId, reason }, \"run stopped and audit delivery failed\");\n    }\n     1\timport { GetSecretValueCommand, SecretsManagerClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\";\n     2\timport { env } from \"../config.js\";\n     3\t\n     4\t// Outbound SMS. One sending number per clinic. Templates are the only bodies sms__send_to_patient\n     5\t// can send; free-form text goes through sms__send_freeform, which needs approval.\n     6\t\n     7\tconst sm = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: env.region });\n     8\tconst BASE = process.env.SMS_API ?? \"https://api.sms-provider.example/v1\";\n     9\t\n    10\texport const TEMPLATES = {\n    11\t  reminder: \"Hi {firstName}, reminder: {when} at {location}. Reply Y to confirm or call us to change.\",\n    12\t  booked: \"Hi {firstName}, you're booked for {when} at {location}.\",\n    13\t  rescheduled: \"Hi {firstName}, your appointment moved to {when} at {location}.\",\n    14\t  cancelled: \"Hi {firstName}, your appointment on {when} is cancelled.\",\n    15\t} as const;\n    16\texport type TemplateId = keyof typeof TEMPLATES;\n    17\t\n    18\texport function render(id: TemplateId, vars: Record<string, string>): string {\n    19\t  return TEMPLATES[id].replace(/\\{(\\w+)\\}/g, (_, k: string) => (vars[k] ?? \"\").replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N} .,:'/-]/gu, \"\").slice(0, 60));\n    20\t}\n    21\t\n    22\tasync function creds(clinicId: string): Promise<{ token: string; from: string }> {\n    23\t  const s = await sm.send(new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId: `clinic-agent/sms/${clinicId}` }));\n    24\t  const v = JSON.parse(s.SecretString ?? \"{}\");\n    25\t  return { token: v.api_token, from: v.from_number };\n    26\t}\n    27\t\n    28\texport const sms = {\n    29\t  async send(clinicId: string, to: string, body: string, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<{ messageId: string }> {\n    30\t    const c = await creds(clinicId);\n    31\t    const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/messages`, {\n    32\t      method: \"POST\",\n    33\t      signal,\n    34\t      headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${c.token}`, \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n    35\t      body: JSON.stringify({ from: c.from, to, body }),\n    36\t    });\n    37\t    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`sms send failed: ${res.status}`);\n    38\t    return (await res.json()) as { messageId: string };\n    39\t  },\n    40\t};\n56:export class AuditUnavailable extends Error {}\n57:\n58:export const audit = {\n59:  async record(e: Omit<AuditEvent, \"eventId\" | \"ts\">): Promise<void> {\n60:    const full = AuditEvent.parse({ ...e, eventId: randomUUID(), ts: new Date().toISOString() });\n61:    try {\n62:      await firehose.send(\n63:        new PutRecordCommand({\n64:          DeliveryStreamName: env.auditStream,\n65:          Record: { Data: Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(full) + \"\\n\") },\n66:        }),\n67:      );\n68:    } catch (err) {\n69:      // Callers treat this as a hard failure: an action that cannot be audited does not run.\n70:      throw new AuditUnavailable(`audit delivery fai