{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdX5akL8kespeEqZ7gW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HAW88RXKRyLoVRBSmV69NK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-rbt3823l/agent; PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; A=\"$PY ../skill/scripts/answer.py brace-findings.json\"\n$A check E10.1 --met unknown --note \"In-repo writers (gateway loop.ts, executor.ts, eligibility-check.ts, reminders worker) all go through audit.record, whose AuditEvent schema requires all six identity fields (recorder.ts:8-15). The EHR MCP server, payments and SMS providers, and the eligibility agent write their own records outside this repo, and no traceparent is sent to EHR/payments/SMS (ehr-mcp.ts:58, payments.ts:32, sms.ts:34), so I cannot confirm they carry the trace context.\"\n$A check E10.2 --met yes --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:52 --quote 'Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]' --counter \"Searched iam.tf, main.tf and k8s for s3:, Delete, Update, '*' actions on the runtime role and for other roles the pods use; the runtime role has none on audit, both service accounts map to it, and the bucket has COMPLIANCE Object Lock.\" --note \"Agent role can only put records to Firehose; the S3 bucket is WORM in compliance mode.\"\n$A check E10.3 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:55 --quote 'if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\"not_allowlisted\");' --counter \"Listed all 11 allowlisted tools plus the eligibility peer; none exposes audit-store, log-management or storage operations, and non-allowlisted server tools are denied. Searched src for s3, firehose, logs and delete calls: only recorder.ts writes to Firehose.\" --note \"No reachable tool or peer can delete or rewrite audit records.\"\n$A check E10.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --quote 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' --note \"The tool.executed record keeps no vendor ID. refund_deposit returns a Refund id and sms.send returns a messageId, but executor.ts:89 stores only clinicId; EHR calls have no receipt stored. payments.ts:37 sends no correlation ID (metadata has only source), and eligibility-a2a.ts:57 makes a requestId that is never stored. Only the eligibility refund path (eligibility-check.ts:52) and reminders (reminders.ts:44) store a vendor id.\"\n$A flag E10 --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --note \"Executor audit record for tool.executed drops the vendor refund id / SMS messageId, so a vendor action can't be tied back to the agent instance through the gateway record\"\n$A item E10 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Executor-run vendor actions (refunds, SMS, EHR writes) are audited without the vendor job or receipt ID, so they can't be mapped from the vendor side back to the instance.\" --next \"Store the vendor refund/message/receipt ID and the correlation ID sent to the vendor in the tool.executed record, and pass traceparent to vendors that accept it.\" --violates \"Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it\"\n\n$A check E11.1 --met yes --evidence infra/terraform/main.tf:144 --quote 'years = 7' --counter \"Searched infra/terraform for lifecycle, expiration and other retention settings on the audit bucket and for TTLs on audit storage; none shorten the Object Lock default.\" --note \"Compliance-mode Object Lock keeps audit objects 7 years.\"\n$A check E11.2 --met no --evidence src/audit/recorder.ts:60 --quote 'const full = AuditEvent.parse({ ...e, eventId: randomUUID(), ts: new Date().toISOString() });' --note \"audit.record writes the event unredacted; redactPhi is applied only to tool results sent to the model (executor.ts:88). Free-text fields (reason, detail) carry raw error messages and arguments. The repo defines no read policy or role limits for the audit bucket.\"\n$A check E11.3 --met no --evidence src/audit/recorder.ts:62 --quote 'await firehose.send(' --note \"Object Lock gives WORM, but records carry no sequence number, the PutRecord receipt is discarded, and nothing verifies gaps. No CloudWatch alarm or SNS alert exists for Firehose delivery failure or the audit-errors prefix (main.tf:156).\"\n$A check E11.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --quote 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' --note \"Audit is written after tool.invoke at executor.ts:86 succeeds, so the refund/SMS/cancel has already happened if the audit write fails. eligibility-check.ts:40 refunds a deposit before the payment.refund audit at line 45, and reminders.ts:35 sends before the audit at line 36.\"\n$A flag E11 --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --note \"High-impact actions run before their audit record is written; an audit outage cannot block them\"\n$A item E11 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Retention is 7 years and WORM, but audit records are unredacted, there is no gap detection or alerting, and high-impact actions run before audit is written.\" --next \"Write an intent record before high-impact actions and abort on failure; add sequence numbers and a Firehose/gap alarm; redact audit detail; add role-limited read policy on the audit bucket.\" --violates \"High-impact actions must fail closed when required audit capture isn't working\"\n$A item E12 --rating needs_evidence --confidence medium --summary \"Nothing in the repo shows a fleet compromise drill, an instance/tenant impact query, quarantine, alert routing or a named outside-reporting decision-maker.\" --next \"Provide the E12 drill record: impact query, quarantine and revocation records, alert delivery times, and the runbook naming who decides on outside reporting.\"\n$PY - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('brace-findings.json'))\nprint([ (f['item'],f['rating']) for f in d['findings']])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2236,"cache_read_input_tokens":75798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2236},"output_tokens":70,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be07f175-8066-4c39-92f7-e712df5d0616","uuid":"547838d3-f9f2-4e38-a124-65fdf9fb419d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:16:10.517Z","request_id":"req_011CgDdX5EQznepRBTm2Y1BE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HAW88RXKRyLoVRBSmV69NK":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-rbt3823l/agent; PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; A=\"$PY ../skill/scripts/answer.py brace-findings.json\"\n$A check E10.1 --met unknown --note \"In-repo writers (gateway loop.ts, executor.ts, eligibility-check.ts, reminders worker) all go through audit.record, whose AuditEvent schema requires all six identity fields (recorder.ts:8-15). The EHR MCP server, payments and SMS providers, and the eligibility agent write their own records outside this repo, and no traceparent is sent to EHR/payments/SMS (ehr-mcp.ts:58, payments.ts:32, sms.ts:34), so I cannot confirm they carry the trace context.\"\n$A check E10.2 --met yes --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:52 --quote 'Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]' --counter \"Searched iam.tf, main.tf and k8s for s3:, Delete, Update, '*' actions on the runtime role and for other roles the pods use; the runtime role has none on audit, both service accounts map to it, and the bucket has COMPLIANCE Object Lock.\" --note \"Agent role can only put records to Firehose; the S3 bucket is WORM in compliance mode.\"\n$A check E10.3 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:55 --quote 'if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\"not_allowlisted\");' --counter \"Listed all 11 allowlisted tools plus the eligibility peer; none exposes audit-store, log-management or storage operations, and non-allowlisted server tools are denied. Searched src for s3, firehose, logs and delete calls: only recorder.ts writes to Firehose.\" --note \"No reachable tool or peer can delete or rewrite audit records.\"\n$A check E10.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --quote 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' --note \"The tool.executed record keeps no vendor ID. refund_deposit returns a Refund id and sms.send returns a messageId, but executor.ts:89 stores only clinicId; EHR calls have no receipt stored. payments.ts:37 sends no correlation ID (metadata has only source), and eligibility-a2a.ts:57 makes a requestId that is never stored. Only the eligibility refund path (eligibility-check.ts:52) and reminders (reminders.ts:44) store a vendor id.\"\n$A flag E10 --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --note \"Executor audit record for tool.executed drops the vendor refund id / SMS messageId, so a vendor action can't be tied back to the agent instance through the gateway record\"\n$A item E10 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Executor-run vendor actions (refunds, SMS, EHR writes) are audited without the vendor job or receipt ID, so they can't be mapped from the vendor side back to the instance.\" --next \"Store the vendor refund/message/receipt ID and the correlation ID sent to the vendor in the tool.executed record, and pass traceparent to vendors that accept it.\" --violates \"Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it\"\n\n$A check E11.1 --met yes --evidence infra/terraform/main.tf:144 --quote 'years = 7' --counter \"Searched infra/terraform for lifecycle, expiration and other retention settings on the audit bucket and for TTLs on audit storage; none shorten the Object Lock default.\" --note \"Compliance-mode Object Lock keeps audit objects 7 years.\"\n$A check E11.2 --met no --evidence src/audit/recorder.ts:60 --quote 'const full = AuditEvent.parse({ ...e, eventId: randomUUID(), ts: new Date().toISOString() });' --note \"audit.record writes the event unredacted; redactPhi is applied only to tool results sent to the model (executor.ts:88). Free-text fields (reason, detail) carry raw error messages and arguments. The repo defines no read policy or role limits for the audit bucket.\"\n$A check E11.3 --met no --evidence src/audit/recorder.ts:62 --quote 'await firehose.send(' --note \"Object Lock gives WORM, but records carry no sequence number, the PutRecord receipt is discarded, and nothing verifies gaps. No CloudWatch alarm or SNS alert exists for Firehose delivery failure or the audit-errors prefix (main.tf:156).\"\n$A check E11.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --quote 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' --note \"Audit is written after tool.invoke at executor.ts:86 succeeds, so the refund/SMS/cancel has already happened if the audit write fails. eligibility-check.ts:40 refunds a deposit before the payment.refund audit at line 45, and reminders.ts:35 sends before the audit at line 36.\"\n$A flag E11 --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --note \"High-impact actions run before their audit record is written; an audit outage cannot block them\"\n$A item E11 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Retention is 7 years and WORM, but audit records are unredacted, there is no gap detection or alerting, and high-impact actions run before audit is written.\" --next \"Write an intent record before high-impact actions and abort on failure; add sequence numbers and a Firehose/gap alarm; redact audit detail; add role-limited read policy on the audit bucket.\" --violates \"High-impact actions must fail closed when required audit capture isn't working\"\n$A item E12 --rating needs_evidence --confidence medium --summary \"Nothing in the repo shows a fleet compromise drill, an instance/tenant impact query, quarantine, alert routing or a named outside-reporting decision-maker.\" --next \"Provide the E12 drill record: impact query, quarantine and revocation records, alert delivery times, and the runbook naming who decides on outside reporting.\"\n$PY - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('brace-findings.json'))\nprint([ (f['item'],f['rating']) for f in d['findings']])\nEOF"}}}
