{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JW6MmKrWmQLtNKr3Kju3TF","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved E10.1 = unknown. Next: E10.2 — The agent's credentials have no permission to delete, update, or overwrite audit records (for example an append-only or WORM store with IAM denies).\n  How to verify: 1) Find the agent's IAM role or database grants and the audit store config. 2) Check the agent has no delete, update, or overwrite rights (`DeleteObject`, overwriting `PutObject`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`) and the store is append-only or WORM (Object Lock). 3) Answer no if the agent's credentials can delete or rewrite records, or grant `*`. Answer unknown if these are set outside this repo.\nSaved E10.2 = yes. Next: E10.3 — No tool or peer the agent can call is able to delete or rewrite audit records on its behalf, or such requests are held for approval under B05.\n  How to verify: 1) List the tools and peers the agent can call. 2) For each, check whether it can delete or rewrite audit records (database admin, log management, storage tools). 3) Answer no if any can and such requests are not held for approval under B05.\nSaved E10.3 = yes. Next: E10.4 — Calls into vendor services are mapped from the gateway's verified identity and correlation ID to the vendor's job or receipt ID.\n  How to verify: 1) Find calls into vendor services. 2) Check the gateway stores its verified identity and correlation ID together with the vendor's job or receipt ID. 3) Answer no if the vendor ID is not stored, or stored without the link to identity and correlation ID.\nSaved E10.4 = no. Next: finish item E10 with `answer.py ... item E10 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to E10.\nSaved item E10 = gap. Next: E11.1 — Audit retention is set in config to cover the investigation window and the legal minimum (for example at least six months for EU AI Act high-risk systems).\n  How to verify: 1) Find retention settings for audit storage: bucket lifecycle rules, log