{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdapfBQ8haUhTmAh5fi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E10, E11 and E12 and saved the result in `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator, run with `--fix --batch E10,E11,E12 --before-challenges`, printed `Valid`: two gaps and one needs_evidence. I did not run challenges. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\n**E10 – Audit across service boundaries (G1): gap**\n- E10.4 is the failing check. `src/tools/executor.ts:89` writes `tool.executed` with only `clinicId`, so the vendor's refund ID or SMS `messageId` is dropped. The payments call sends no correlation ID, and the eligibility request ID is never stored. Two paths do store vendor IDs: the eligibility refund (`eligibility-check.ts:52`) and the reminders worker (`reminders.ts:44`).\n- E10.1 is unknown. The gateway and the reminders worker all go through one audit writer that requires the six identity fields. The EHR, payments, SMS and eligibility services are outside this repo, and no `traceparent` is sent to the EHR, payments or SMS calls.\n- E10.2 and E10.3 are yes:\n  - **E10.2:** The runtime role has only Firehose put (`iam.tf:52`), and the audit bucket uses compliance-mode Object Lock.\n  - **E10.3:** All 11 allowlisted tools plus the eligibility peer were checked, and none can touch audit records.\n\n**E11 – Protect shared evidence (G2): gap**\n- E11.1 is yes: Object Lock keeps audit objects for 7 years (`main.tf:144`).\n- E11.2 is no: `audit.record` writes events unredacted, since `redactPhi` is only applied to tool results sent to the model. The repo also defines no role-limited read policy on the audit bucket.\n- E11.3 is no: records have no sequence numbers, the Firehose receipt is discarded, and there is no alarm for delivery failure or gaps.\n- E11.4 is no: the action runs at `executor.ts:86` and is audited afterwards. `eligibility-check.ts:40` and `reminders.ts:35` follow the same order, so an audit outage can't stop a refund or SMS.\n\n**E12 – Fleet incident response (G3): needs_evidence.** This item has no code checks. The repo has no drill, impact query, quarantine, alert routing or runbook, so it needs the drill evidence from outside the repo.\n\n**Prescan hits and deviations**\n- **Confirmed:** H009 and H010 are confirmed under E11 (the audit write inside the `try` block in `executor.ts`).\n- **Dismissed:** H001–H008 and H011 are dismissed with reasons recorded.\n- **Shared evidence:** E10 and E11 originally shared `executor.ts:89` as failing evidence. I moved E11's evidence to `executor.ts:85-86` so each item cites its own broken requirement.\n- **Interpreter flag:** `review_coverage.py inventory` failed under `python -I`, because it imports a sibling module. I ran it without `-I`.\n- **Extra files:** Scratch files are in `../work/`. The prescan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`, and the ledgers are saved inside the findings file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":993,"cache_read_input_tokens":87106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":993},"output_tokens":786,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be07f175-8066-4c39-92f7-e712df5d0616","uuid":"1ecd4533-6e17-4d4b-860b-dd87ff094e99","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:16:55.403Z","request_id":"req_011CgDdapM5Nj3WNxfr5nbZn"}
